UID:10004676-1790240400-1790244000@www.engineering.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Research Round: Extending the Utility of a Digital Microfluidic Based Omics (DISCO) Platform for Single Cell Proteomics
DESCRIPTION:Savina Cammalleri is a Ph.D. student at the U of T’s Institute of Biomedical Engineering and is currently conducting her research at the Max Planck Institute for Multidisciplinary Sciences within the Molecular Neurobiology Group. \nHer work explores the extension of a digital microfluidic-based single cell omics (DISCO) platform for single-cell proteomics. By leveraging digital microfluidics to manipulate individual cells and samples\, the platform aims to enable more efficient and scalable analysis of proteins at the single-cell level. \nThis research has the potential to expand the capabilities of single-cell proteomics by providing a flexible approach for studying cellular heterogeneity and molecular processes. By further developing the DISCO platform\, Savina’s work aims to contribute new tools for high-resolution biological analysis and ultimately advance our understanding of complex cellular systems. \nRegister Here
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/research-round-extending-the-utility-of-a-digital-microfluidic-based-omics-disco-platform-for-single-cell-proteomics/
LOCATION:Zoom
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
